-- Q1051: IT General Controls [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ITIL 4 Section 5.2 (Change Enablement) and COBIT 2019 BAI06, emergency changes bypass normal pre-approval but must be retroactively documented, tested, and formally approved by the Change Advisory Board. This ensures governance is maintained while allowing rapid response to critical outages.
Wrong (A): Emergency changes are not automatically approved simply because they addressed a critical issue; retroactive review and formal approval are still required.
Wrong (C): The developer who deployed the fix cannot also approve it, as this violates segregation of duties in change management.
Wrong (D): Emergency changes are not exempt from all change control requirements; they follow an expedited process with mandatory post-implementation review.$EXPL$
