UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under COBIT 2019 Section EDM01 and ITIL 4 Section 4.1, COBIT provides the governance structure and strategic objectives (the "what") while ITIL provides detailed operational service management practices (the "how"). Organizations commonly deploy both for complementary coverage.
Wrong (A): COBIT and ITIL are complementary, not competing frameworks; they address different layers of IT management and are designed to work together.
Wrong (B): COBIT addresses enterprise-wide IT governance, not just security, and ITIL addresses service management, not project management.
