-- Q1065: IT Audit Frameworks [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under COBIT 2019 Section APO12 (Manage Risk), the risk owner should compare residual risk against the organization''s defined risk appetite and tolerance levels to determine whether additional controls or treatment is warranted. Even with strong controls, moderate residual risk may exceed the acceptable threshold.
Wrong (A): Immediately eliminating the risk by discontinuing the business activity is an extreme response that ignores cost-benefit analysis and the possibility that residual risk is within tolerance.
Wrong (C): Strong current controls do not automatically mean residual risk is acceptable; the risk owner must verify alignment with the board-approved risk appetite before concluding.
Wrong (D): Transferring all residual risk regardless of cost is impractical and ignores the principle that risk treatment decisions must be cost-justified relative to the risk level.$EXPL$
