-- Q1219: SOC Reporting [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AT-C 205, an adverse opinion is issued when exceptions are so widespread and significant that the control environment as a whole cannot be relied upon. The subject matter departs materially and pervasively from the applicable trust services criteria.
Wrong (A): No exceptions during testing would result in an unqualified (clean) opinion, not an adverse opinion.
Wrong (B): Inability to obtain sufficient evidence to form an opinion leads to a disclaimer of opinion, not an adverse opinion.
Wrong (D): The report''s coverage period does not determine the opinion type; opinions are based on the severity and pervasiveness of control exceptions found during testing.$EXPL$
