-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): A bridge letter (gap letter) is a management representation from the service organization covering the period between the SOC report end date and the user entity''s fiscal year-end, per SSAE 18 (AT-C Section 320). It addresses whether significant changes occurred to the system or controls during the gap period.
Wrong (A): A bridge letter is a management representation, not an independent examination, and provides less assurance than a SOC report.
Wrong (B): A bridge letter does not eliminate the need for additional audit procedures; user auditors may still need to perform supplementary procedures based on their risk assessment.
Wrong (C): A bridge letter is not a request to extend the SOC report period; it is a separate management assertion covering the gap between the report end date and the user''s year-end.$EXPL$
